# etude-5dr.7 plan

Reject two final caller-guard topology bypasses without widening product scope. First, bind Git control snapshots to both resolved path and regular-file content so replacing `.git/config` with a same-byte symlink changes the snapshot and fails before publication. Second, walk every parent component of each tracked path with `Lstat` and reject non-directory or symlink ancestors before hashing the leaf, so identical bytes reached through an ignored symlinked directory cannot pass. Add independent no-publication regressions, document both restrictions, then rerun the full suite and fresh built-binary QA.
